{
  "AIF": {
    "nodes": [
      {
        "nodeID": 1,
        "type": "L",
        "text": "Aristotle: perhaps we shall find the best good if we first find the function of a human being"
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 2,
        "type": "I",
        "text": "The function of a human being should be found first, to find the best good",
        "pta": {
          "subject": "the function of a human being",
          "predicate": "should be found first, to find the best good",
          "kind": "P",
          "scope": "u"
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 3,
        "type": "YA",
        "text": "Asserting",
        "pta": {
          "transformations": [
            "illocution substitution",
            "passivization"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 4,
        "type": "L",
        "text": "Aristotle: the good, i.e., ‹doing› well, for a flautist, a sculptor, and every craftsman, and, in general, for whatever has a function and ‹characteristic› action, seems to depend on its function"
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 5,
        "type": "I",
        "text": "The good of a flautist, a sculptor and every craftsman depends on its function",
        "pta": {
          "subject": "the good of a flautist, a sculptor and every craftsman",
          "predicate": "depends on its function",
          "kind": "F",
          "scope": "p"
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 6,
        "type": "I",
        "text": "The good of whatever has a function depends on its function",
        "pta": {
          "subject": "the good of whatever has a function",
          "predicate": "depends on its function",
          "kind": "F",
          "scope": "u"
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 7,
        "type": "YA",
        "text": "Asserting"
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 8,
        "type": "YA",
        "text": "Asserting",
        "pta": {
          "transformations": [
            "explication"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 9,
        "type": "L",
        "text": "Aristotle: the same seems to be true for a human being, if a human being has some function"
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 10,
        "type": "I",
        "text": "The good of a human being depends on its function",
        "pta": {
          "subject": "the good of a human being",
          "predicate": "depends on its function",
          "kind": "F",
          "scope": "u"
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 11,
        "type": "I",
        "text": "The function of a human being is what the good of a human being depends on",
        "pta": {
          "subject": "the function of a human being",
          "predicate": "is what the good of a human being depends on",
          "kind": "F",
          "scope": "u"
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 12,
        "type": "YA",
        "text": "Asserting",
        "pta": {
          "transformations": [
            "anaphora"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 13,
        "type": "YA",
        "text": "Asserting",
        "pta": {
          "transformations": [
            "anaphora",
            "passivization"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 14,
        "type": "L",
        "text": "Aristotle: do the carpenter and the leatherworker have their functions and actions, while a human being has none, and is by nature idle, without any function"
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 15,
        "type": "I",
        "text": "A human being has a function",
        "pta": {
          "subject": "a human being",
          "predicate": "has a function",
          "kind": "F",
          "scope": "u"
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 16,
        "type": "I",
        "text": "The carpenter and the leatherworker have a function",
        "pta": {
          "subject": "the carpenter and the leatherworker",
          "predicate": "has a function",
          "kind": "F",
          "scope": "p"
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 17,
        "type": "YA",
        "text": "Rhetorical Questioning",
        "pta": {
          "transformations": [
            "illocution substitution"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 18,
        "type": "YA",
        "text": "Asserting",
        "pta": {
          "transformations": [
            "same term"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 19,
        "type": "L",
        "text": "Aristotle: just as eye, hand, foot and, in general, every ‹bodily› part apparently has its functions"
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 20,
        "type": "I",
        "text": "Eye, hand and foot have a function",
        "pta": {
          "subject": "eye, hand and foot",
          "predicate": "has a function",
          "kind": "F",
          "scope": "p"
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 21,
        "type": "I",
        "text": "Every bodily part has a function",
        "pta": {
          "subject": "every bodily part",
          "predicate": "has a function",
          "kind": "F",
          "scope": "u"
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 22,
        "type": "YA",
        "text": "Asserting",
        "pta": {
          "transformations": [
            "same term"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 23,
        "type": "YA",
        "text": "Asserting",
        "pta": {
          "transformations": [
            "same term"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 24,
        "type": "L",
        "text": "Aristotle: may we likewise ascribe to a human being some function apart from all of theirs"
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 25,
        "type": "YA",
        "text": "Rhetorical Questioning",
        "pta": {
          "transformations": [
            "illocution substitution",
            "activization"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 26,
        "type": "L",
        "text": "Aristotle: living is apparently shared with plants"
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 27,
        "type": "I",
        "text": "The life of nutrition and growth is shared with plants",
        "pta": {
          "subject": "the life of nutrition and growth",
          "predicate": "is shared with plants",
          "kind": "F",
          "scope": "s"
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 28,
        "type": "YA",
        "text": "Asserting",
        "pta": {
          "transformations": [
            "same term"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 29,
        "type": "L",
        "text": "Aristotle: what we are looking for is the special function of a human being"
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 30,
        "type": "I",
        "text": "The function of a human being is special to a human being",
        "pta": {
          "subject": "the function of a human being",
          "predicate": "is special to a human being",
          "kind": "F",
          "scope": "u"
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 31,
        "type": "YA",
        "text": "Asserting",
        "pta": {
          "transformations": [
            "explication"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 32,
        "type": "L",
        "text": "Aristotle: we should set aside the life of nutrition and growth"
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 33,
        "type": "I",
        "text": "The life of nutrition and growth is not the special function of a human being",
        "pta": {
          "subject": "the life of nutrition and growth",
          "predicate": "is not the special function of a human being",
          "kind": "F",
          "scope": "s"
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 34,
        "type": "YA",
        "text": "Asserting",
        "pta": {
          "transformations": [
            "illocution substitution"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 35,
        "type": "L",
        "text": "Aristotle: The life next in order is some sort of life of sense-perception"
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 36,
        "type": "I",
        "text": "The life of sense-perception is next in order",
        "pta": {
          "subject": "the life of sense-perception",
          "predicate": "is next in order",
          "kind": "F",
          "scope": "s"
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 37,
        "type": "YA",
        "text": "Asserting",
        "pta": {
          "transformations": [
            "passivization"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 38,
        "type": "L",
        "text": "Aristotle: this too is apparently shared, with horse, ox and every animal"
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 39,
        "type": "I",
        "text": "The life of sense-perception is shared with every animal",
        "pta": {
          "subject": "the life of sense-perception",
          "predicate": "is shared with every animal",
          "kind": "F",
          "scope": "s"
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 40,
        "type": "YA",
        "text": "Asserting",
        "pta": {
          "transformations": [
            "anaphora"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 41,
        "type": "I",
        "text": "The life of sense-perception is not the special function of a human being",
        "pta": {
          "subject": "the life of sense-perception",
          "predicate": "is not the special function of a human being",
          "kind": "F",
          "scope": "s",
          "note": "implicit: the second elimination, by the same lever as the first"
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 42,
        "type": "L",
        "text": "Aristotle: The remaining possibility, then, is some sort of life of action of the ‹part of the soul› that has reason"
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 43,
        "type": "I",
        "text": "The life of action of the part of the soul that has reason is the remaining possibility for the special function of a human being",
        "pta": {
          "subject": "the life of action of the part of the soul that has reason",
          "predicate": "is the remaining possibility for the special function of a human being",
          "kind": "V",
          "scope": "s"
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 44,
        "type": "YA",
        "text": "Asserting",
        "pta": {
          "transformations": [
            "passivization",
            "explication"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 45,
        "type": "I",
        "text": "The life of action of the part of the soul that has reason is the only kind of life not shared with plants or animals",
        "pta": {
          "subject": "the life of action of the part of the soul that has reason",
          "predicate": "is the only kind of life not shared with plants or animals",
          "kind": "F",
